.TH "hyprctl" "1" "" "" "hyprctl User Manual"
.SH NAME
hyprctl \- Utility for controlling parts of Hypoland from a CLI or a
script
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]hyprctl\f[R] [\f[I](opt)flags\f[R]] [\f[B]command\f[R]]
[\f[I](opt)args\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]hyprctl\f[R] is a utility for controlling some parts of the
compositor from a CLI or a script.
.SH CONTROL COMMANDS
\f[B]dispatch\f[R]
.RS
.PP
Call a dispatcher with an argument.
.PP
An argument must be present.
For dispatchers without parameters it can be anything.
.PP
Returns: \f[I]ok\f[R] on success, and an error message on failure.
.TP
Examples:
\f[B]hyprctl\f[R] \f[I]dispatch
\(dqhl.dsp.exec_cmd(\(aqkitty\(aq)\(dq\f[R]
.RS
.PP
\f[B]hyprctl\f[R] \f[I]dispatch \(dqhl.dsp.window.close()\(dq\f[R]
.RE
.RE
.PP
\f[B]keyword\f[R]
.RS
.PP
Not available: the config is Lua, the compositor answers \f[I]unknown
request\f[R].
Use \f[B]eval\f[R] instead, e.g.
\f[I]eval \(aqhl.config({ general = { border_size = 10 } })\(aq\f[R].
.RE
.PP
\f[B]eval\f[R]
.RS
.PP
Evaluate arbitrary Lua expressions dynamically when using a Lua\-based
config provider.
.PP
Returns: \f[I]ok\f[R] on success, and an error message on failure.
.TP
Examples:
\f[B]hyprctl\f[R] \f[I]eval \(aqhl.bind(\(dqSUPER + SHIFT + Q\(dq,
hl.dsp.exec_cmd(\(dqfirefox\(dq))\(aq\f[R]
.RS
.PP
\f[B]hyprctl\f[R] \f[I]eval \(aqhl.config({ general = { border_size = 10
} })\(aq\f[R]
.RE
.RE
.PP
\f[B]reload\f[R]
.RS
.PP
Force a reload of the config file.
.RE
.PP
\f[B]kill\f[R]
.RS
.PP
Enter kill mode, where you can kill an app by clicking on it.
You can exit by pressing ESCAPE.
.RE
